    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter June 1st looking to maximize efficiency in a landscape where stolen base upside remains our primary engine. **Christian Yelich** is our undeniable anchor today, boasting a 63.76 score against Landen Roupp. While Roupp presents a moderate challenge, **Christian Yelich** benefits from a massive 13% dynamic platoon boost and the premium value of the leadoff spot, making him the only \"Strong\" play on the board. **Carson Benge** (54.69) and **Colt Keith** (50.24) follow as solid options; **Colt Keith** is particularly interesting because we are betting on his speed to exploit the slow delivery of Griffin Jax, which provides a small but crucial +2% boost to his SB probability in a category where we refuse to concede ground.\n\nNavigating the remainder of the roster requires balancing marginal gains against game cap preservation. **Junior Caminero** (48.90) faces a stiff test against Ty Madden\u2019s 2.31 xERA, suppressing his total significantly despite his base talent. Meanwhile, **Luke Raley** (44.99) and **Gary Sanchez** (43.82) are functioning as high-floor bench-fillers today; their scores hover just above our threshold, and they are starts primarily due to the lack of high-upside alternatives. **Chase Meidroth** was our closest exclusion, missing the cut with a 36.86 score. While he held a decent park factor, he ultimately couldn't overcome the efficiency penalty of facing an elite arm like Joe Ryan, who suppressed his projection too far for us to justify a spot over our current starters. \n\nAll participants should be aware that these projections are built on \"Lineup Pending\" assumptions. Should **Colt Keith** or **Christian Yelich** be shifted down the order once official cards are posted, their value\u2014and our expected output\u2014will fluctuate rapidly. We are also monitoring the heavy SP xERAs across the board; with several of our hitters facing pitchers with an xERA under 3.80, the risk of a low-scoring day is elevated. Bench options like **Dillon Dingler** and **Casey Schmitt** remain ready, but until we see favorable lineup placements and better platoon splits, they will remain safely sidelined to preserve our season-long game caps.",
